# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: `mise.toml`'s `"npm:firecrawl-cli"`
#   pinned here:    1.23.3
#
# RESYNCED 2026-09-09. It had drifted to v1.23.1 while `mise.toml` pinned
# 1.23.3, and NOTHING REPORTED IT — `currency.toml` declared no `manifest =`
# row for this tool, so the manifest-vs-pin comparison never ran. The row is
# added in the same change; without it this file can silently drift again.
#
# Found while reviewing why `kb-tool-sync` refuses 15 of 20 tools. The five it
# ACCEPTS are exactly the five with no `manifest =` key — so the tools the
# automated sync can touch were precisely the ones whose provenance nothing was
# checking, and this one was already wrong. Eligibility was inversely correlated
# with coverage.
#
# `commit` came from `manifest.resolve_tag(url, "1.23.3", prefix="v")`, never a
# hand `ls-remote` — see `sources/mise.manifest`'s header for the #395 trap that
# call reproduces, and `sources/codex.manifest` for the day it was walked into
# again.
